As a cause of anxiety for Danny, Bart Beeber, the nerdiest
guy in school, has already found a date.

4
00:17:46,666 --> 00:17:52,666
At the same time, Danny's divorced parents are both seeking relationships again.

5
00:22:13,333 --> 00:22:19,333
Danny, played by Steven Kaplan.

6
00:26:40,000 --> 00:26:46,000
Ernie Stein, played by William H. Macy.

7
00:31:06,666 --> 00:31:12,666
Beth Stein, played by Cheryl Hines.

8
00:35:33,333 --> 00:35:39,333
Alice, played by Ashley Benson.

9
00:40:00,000 --> 00:40:06,000
Camille, played by Alia Shawkat.

10
00:44:26,666 --> 00:44:32,666
Craig, played by Brandon Hardesty.

11
00:48:53,333 --> 00:48:59,333
Bart Got a Room is a 2008 comedy film written and directed by Brian
Hecker, and stars Steven Kaplan, Alia Shawkat, William H.

12
00:53:20,000 --> 00:53:26,000
Macy, and Cheryl Hines.

13
00:57:46,666 --> 00:57:52,666
Also appearing in the film are Ashley Benson, Brandon Hardesty, Kate Micucci, Jennifer Tilly,
Dinah Manoff (in her last film role as of 2022) and Chad Jamian Williams as Bart.

14
01:02:13,333 --> 01:02:19,333
The film premiered at the Tribeca Film Festival on April 25, 2008.

15
01:06:40,000 --> 01:06:46,000
It had a limited US release in select theaters on April 3,
2009, and was released on DVD on July 28, 2009.

16
01:11:06,666 --> 01:11:12,666
The film explores themes of high school, date,
coming of age, prom, divorced parents.

17
01:15:33,333 --> 01:15:39,333
The tone is lighthearted and emotional.
